{
  "email": "aisha.khan@brightline.example",
  "reason": "KB-008 quick check: see if payroll verification phishing was caught"
}

{
  "summary": "Reported: Aisha Khan (HR, user_id 5) asks whether an email \"going around\" asking staff to verify their payroll login is real. She says she heard about it from others, so it may have reached several users. Checked: her account is active with 0 failed sign-ins and no block. Her quarantine has Q-1003, from it-support@brightIine-help.example (lookalike domain: capital I in place of l), subject \"Urgent: verify your payroll login\", received 2026-10-09 08:52 UTC, marked phishing and not releasable. It was caught before reaching her inbox, and nothing suggests she clicked it. Why escalating: KB-008 says to escalate when several users get the same message, and her report suggests a campaign across the company. Still needed: security should check how widely it was delivered, find any copies that got past the filter into inboxes, block the brightIine-help.example sender/domain, and check whether anyone clicked or entered credentials (KB-029). A company-wide warning may be worth sending. Told the user: it's phishing, don't click, use Report Phishing if a copy shows up, and contact us right away if she ever entered credentials.",
  "reason": "KB-008: likely sent to several users (user says it's 'going around'); lookalike domain phishing campaign"
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Aisha, thanks for checking before acting. That email is not real. It's a phishing attempt. It comes from an address made to look like ours, but if you look closely it's \"brightIine\" with a capital I, not \"brightline\". Our filters caught your copy before it reached your inbox, so you're fine, and your payroll isn't affected. If a copy ever does show up in your inbox, don't click, reply, or forward it. Use the Report Phishing button in Outlook, then delete it. If you or anyone you know clicked the link or typed a password into it, tell us right away so we can secure the account. I've passed this to our security team so they can check who else got it.",
  "internal_note": "Looked up the user: Aisha Khan, user_id 5, HR, account active, 0 failed sign-ins. Her quarantine has Q-1003, from it-support@brightIine-help.example (lookalike domain), subject \"Urgent: verify your payroll login\", received 2026-10-09 08:52 UTC. It's marked phishing and is not releasable. It never reached her inbox and she hasn't reported clicking anything, so KB-029 doesn't apply to her. Escalated to Tier 2/security (escalation 1) under KB-008 because she says the email is \"going around\", which points to a campaign hitting several users. Recommend checking how widely it was delivered, blocking the domain, and looking for anyone who clicked. Her quarantine also has two ordinary spam messages (Q-1001, Q-1002). She didn't ask about them, so I took no action.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-008"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
